title: Seals, mesh, frame
from: Zainab Kovac
gist: Kovac's small talk on stripping a scrubber: the order, the spanners, and the real time.
== lines
kovac-zainab: Oh. Um. Hello. That's a lot of chairs. Sorry. Right. Scrubbers.   [nod]
kovac-zainab: This is a scrubber filter. It cleans the air you're breathing. Every breath.
kovac-zainab: People say I can strip one in ten minutes flat. That's wrong.   [gesture]
kovac-zainab: It's nine and a half. I've timed it. Forty times.
kovac-zainab: The trick is the order. Seals, then the mesh, then the frame. Never the frame first.
kovac-zainab: And put the spanners back in order. Somebody never does. I won't say who.
kovac-zainab: That's... sorry, that's it. Questions? You don't have to.
